---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Week 8 Quiz: Introduction to Arduino and Hardware">
    <main style="min-height: 100vh; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff3e0 0%, #ffcc80 100%); padding: 3rem 0;">
        <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
            <!-- Header -->
            <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <div style="background: #f57c00; color: white; border-radius: 50%; width: 4rem; height: 4rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-right: 1rem;">Q8</div>
                    <div style="text-align: left;">
                        <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: var(--black); margin: 0;">Week 8 Quiz</h1>
                        <p style="color: var(--gray); margin: 0;">Introduction to Arduino and Hardware</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Quiz Form -->
            <div style="background: white; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); padding: 2rem;">
                <form id="week8Quiz" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem;">
                    <!-- Student Info -->
                    <div style="background: var(--gray-light); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 1rem;">Student Information</h3>
                        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
                            <div>
                                <label style="display: block; font-weight: 500; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Name:</label>
                                <input type="text" id="studentName" style="width: 100%; padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 1rem;" required>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <label style="display: block; font-weight: 500; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Email:</label>
                                <input type="email" id="studentEmail" style="width: 100%; padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 1rem;" required>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Question 1 -->
                    <div style="border-left: 4px solid #f57c00; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Question 1: Multiple Choice (2 points)</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1rem;">What is Arduino?</p>
                        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="a" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>A) A programming language</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="b" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>B) An open-source microcontroller platform</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="c" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>C) A type of sensor</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="d" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>D) A computer operating system</span>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Question 2 -->
                    <div style="border-left: 4px solid #f57c00; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Question 2: Multiple Choice (2 points)</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1rem;">Which functions are required in every Arduino sketch?</p>
                        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="a" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>A) start() and end()</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="b" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>B) setup() and loop()</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="c" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>C) begin() and run()</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="d" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>D) init() and main()</span>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Question 3 -->
                    <div style="border-left: 4px solid #f57c00; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Question 3: Short Answer (3 points)</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1rem;">Write Arduino code to turn on an LED connected to pin 13:</p>
                        <textarea id="q3" name="q3" rows="4" style="width: 100%; padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 6px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.9rem;" placeholder="Type your Arduino code here..."></textarea>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Question 4 -->
                    <div style="border-left: 4px solid #f57c00; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Question 4: True/False (2 points)</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1rem;">Digital pins on Arduino can only output HIGH (5V) or LOW (0V) values.</p>
                        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q4" value="true" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>True</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q4" value="false" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>False</span>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Question 5 -->
                    <div style="border-left: 4px solid #f57c00; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Question 5: Multiple Choice (1 point)</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1rem;">What is the purpose of the setup() function in Arduino?</p>
                        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="a" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>A) It runs continuously in a loop</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="b" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>B) It runs once when the program starts</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="c" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>C) It handles errors</span>
                            </label>
                            <label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
                                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="d" style="margin-right: 0.75rem;">
                                <span>D) It connects to the internet</span>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Submit Button -->
                    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem;">
                        <button type="submit" style="background: #f57c00; color: white; padding: 1rem 2rem; border: none; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; transition: background-color 0.2s;">
                            Submit Quiz
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </form>

                <!-- Results Display -->
                <div id="quizResults" style="display: none; margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: #fff3e0; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: bold; color: #e65100; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Quiz Results</h3>
                    <div id="scoreDisplay" style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"></div>
                    <div id="feedback" style="color: var(--gray);"></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Navigation -->
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-top: 2rem;">
                <a href="/programming/lessons/week8" style="background: #f57c00; color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; transition: background-color 0.2s;">
                    ← Back to Lesson
                </a>
                <a href="/programming/semester1" style="background: var(--gray); color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; transition: background-color 0.2s;">
                    Semester Overview
                </a>
                <a href="/programming/lessons/week9" style="background: #e65100; color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; transition: background-color 0.2s;">
                    Next Lesson →
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@emailjs/browser@4/dist/email.min.js"></script>
    <script>
        // Quiz answers and scoring
        const correctAnswers = {
            q1: 'b',  // open-source microcontroller platform
            q2: 'b',  // setup() and loop()
            q4: 'true',  // digital pins output HIGH/LOW
            q5: 'b'   // setup() runs once at start
        };

        const totalPoints = 10;

        document.getElementById('week8Quiz').addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            
            const studentName = document.getElementById('studentName').value;
            const studentEmail = document.getElementById('studentEmail').value;
            
            if (!studentName || !studentEmail) {
                alert('Please fill in your name and email.');
                return;
            }

            let score = 0;
            let feedback = [];

            // Check Q1 (2 points)
            const q1Answer = document.querySelector('input[name="q1"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement;
            if (q1Answer && q1Answer.value === correctAnswers.q1) {
                score += 2;
                feedback.push('✓ Question 1: Correct - Arduino is an open-source microcontroller platform');
            } else {
                feedback.push('✗ Question 1: Incorrect - Arduino is an open-source microcontroller platform');
            }

            // Check Q2 (2 points)
            const q2Answer = document.querySelector('input[name="q2"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement;
            if (q2Answer && q2Answer.value === correctAnswers.q2) {
                score += 2;
                feedback.push('✓ Question 2: Correct - Arduino uses setup() and loop() functions');
            } else {
                feedback.push('✗ Question 2: Incorrect - Arduino uses setup() and loop() functions');
            }

            // Check Q4 (2 points)
            const q4Answer = document.querySelector('input[name="q4"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement;
            if (q4Answer && q4Answer.value === correctAnswers.q4) {
                score += 2;
                feedback.push('✓ Question 4: Correct - Digital pins output HIGH (5V) or LOW (0V)');
            } else {
                feedback.push('✗ Question 4: Incorrect - Digital pins output HIGH (5V) or LOW (0V)');
            }

            // Check Q5 (2 points)
            const q5Answer = document.querySelector('input[name="q5"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement;
            if (q5Answer && q5Answer.value === correctAnswers.q5) {
                score += 2;
                feedback.push('✓ Question 5: Correct - setup() runs once at start');
            } else {
                feedback.push('✗ Question 5: Incorrect - setup() runs once at start');
            }

            // Check short answer (Q3) - basic validation for Arduino LED code
            const q3Answer = (document.getElementById('q3') as HTMLTextAreaElement).value.toLowerCase().trim();
            if ((q3Answer.includes('pinmode') && q3Answer.includes('13') && q3Answer.includes('output')) &&
                (q3Answer.includes('digitalwrite') && q3Answer.includes('high'))) {
                score += 3;
                feedback.push('✓ Question 3: Correct - Good Arduino LED control code');
            } else {
                feedback.push('✗ Question 3: Missing key elements (pinMode, digitalWrite, pin 13, HIGH)');
            }

            const percentage = Math.round((score / totalPoints) * 100);
            
            // Display results
            (document.getElementById('scoreDisplay') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = `
                <strong>Score: ${score}/${totalPoints} (${percentage}%)</strong>
            `;
            
            (document.getElementById('feedback') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = feedback.join('<br>');
            (document.getElementById('quizResults') as HTMLElement).style.display = 'block';

            // Prepare quiz data for submission
            const quizData = {
                studentName: studentName,
                studentEmail: studentEmail,
                week: 8,
                topic: 'Introduction to Arduino and Hardware',
                score: score,
                totalPoints: totalPoints,
                percentage: percentage,
                answers: {
                    q1: (document.querySelector('input[name="q1"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement)?.value || 'No answer',
                    q2: (document.querySelector('input[name="q2"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement)?.value || 'No answer',
                    q3: (document.getElementById('q3') as HTMLTextAreaElement).value || 'No answer',
                    q4: (document.querySelector('input[name="q4"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement)?.value || 'No answer',
                    q5: (document.querySelector('input[name="q5"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement)?.value || 'No answer'
                },
                submittedAt: new Date().toISOString()
            };

            // Submit to teacher via EmailJS
            emailjs.send('service_ot1jg6s', 'template_io02xtm', {
                to_email: 'chuck@c00lnerd.com',
                from_name: quizData.studentName,
                from_email: quizData.studentEmail,
                message: `WEEK 8 QUIZ RESULTS - INTRODUCTION TO ARDUINO AND HARDWARE

Student Information:
• Name: ${quizData.studentName}
• Email: ${quizData.studentEmail}

Quiz Performance:
• Score: ${quizData.score}/${quizData.totalPoints} (${quizData.percentage}%)
• Topic: ${quizData.topic}
• Submission Date: ${new Date(quizData.submittedAt).toLocaleString()}

Student Responses:
• Q1 (Arduino Definition): ${quizData.answers.q1} ${quizData.answers.q1 === 'b' ? '✓' : '✗'}
• Q2 (Required Functions): ${quizData.answers.q2} ${quizData.answers.q2 === 'b' ? '✓' : '✗'}
• Q3 (LED Control Code): ${quizData.answers.q3}
• Q4 (Digital Pin Values): ${quizData.answers.q4} ${quizData.answers.q4 === 'true' ? '✓' : '✗'}
• Q5 (Setup Function): ${quizData.answers.q5} ${quizData.answers.q5 === 'b' ? '✓' : '✗'}

Performance Analysis:
${quizData.percentage >= 80 ? '🎉 Excellent! Student demonstrates strong understanding of Arduino basics and hardware concepts.' : 
  quizData.percentage >= 70 ? '👍 Good work! Student grasps Arduino fundamentals but may need practice with code syntax.' :
  quizData.percentage >= 60 ? '⚠️ Satisfactory. Student understands basics but needs more practice with Arduino programming.' :
  '📚 Needs improvement. Recommend additional review of Arduino platform, functions, and basic programming.'}`,
                subject: `Week 8 Arduino Quiz - ${quizData.studentName}`
            })
            .then(function(response) {
                console.log('Quiz results sent successfully!', response.status, response.text);
            }, function(error) {
                console.log('Failed to send quiz results...', error);
            });
        });

        // Initialize EmailJS
        emailjs.init("ct_s19oZHppLy9BlW");
    </script>
</Layout>
